{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## All 6 ACs met — closing\n\nFix landed as **`84de45fe265ae9d6c8f41d61460c73532f3e78df`** (\"tests: make doctor repair\nidentity hermetic\"), Gerrit change **2983**, trailer `rebar-ticket: 8c5f-7727-ed1c-4151`.\nVerification was run against a fresh worktree at `origin/main`, not the shared checkout.\n\n### AC1 — reproduce first: MET\n\nAt `84de45fe265^`:\n\n```\n............F..FF.FF..                                                   [100%]\nE  rebar._commands._repair_pause.RepairPauseError: Error: doctor repair requires a\n   configured git user.email\n5 failed, 17 passed in 5.67s\n```\n\nThe 5 measured nodeids, all in `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py`:\n\n```\ntest_repair_force_writes_the_pre_repair_tag_and_repoints_it\ntest_run_repair_does_not_hold_a_lock_that_blocks_its_own_writes\ntest_json_output_carries_the_documented_finding_fields\ntest_repair_refuses_while_a_reconciler_pass_is_in_flight\ntest_unrepairable_finding_leaves_its_edge_and_the_run_continues\n```\n\n### AC2 — all 5 pass after the fix: MET\n\nOn `origin/main`, whole file then the exact AC1 set:\n\n```\n......................        22 passed in 6.42s\n.....                          5 passed in 4.91s\n```\n\nThe 5 re-run nodeids are the measured AC1 set, not transcribed from this description.\n\n### AC3 — the scrub is not weakened: MET\n\n`git show --stat --patch 84de45fe265 -- tests/conftest.py` printed the commit header and\n**no patch** — the landed change does not touch `tests/conftest.py` or the body of\n`scrub_ambient_git_config`. The call site is intact:\n\n```\n168\t    scrub_ambient_git_config(os.environ)\n```\n\nThe four-file identity oracle: `71 passed in 25.93s`.\n\n### AC4 — the helper does not mutate `os.environ`: MET\n\n`configure_repo_git_identity` (`tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py:51-63`) copies the\nenvironment, scrubs the **copy**, and writes **repo-local** config to a caller-supplied path:\n\n```python\nenv = subprocess_env()\nscrub_ambient_git_config(env)\nfor key, value in ((\"user.email\", email), (\"user.name\", name)):\n    subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"-C\", str(repo), \"config\", \"--local\", key, value],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, env=env,\n    )\n```\n\nNo assignment to `os.environ`; no global config. The asserting test exists and passes:\n\n```\ntests/test_sandbox_capabilities_985f.py::test_configure_repo_git_identity_does_not_mutate_os_environ\n.                                                                        [100%]\n1 passed in 0.87s\n```\n\n### AC5 — the latent dependency searched for elsewhere: MET, result set EMPTY\n\nMethod: `grep -RIn '_git_email' src tests`, `grep -RIn 'owned_repair_pause' src tests`, then\nan AST scan over `tests/**/*.py` for unredirected `run_repair`, `doctor_cli --repair`, and\n`bridge_pause` calls. (Serena was not exposed in that session, so this was grep + AST rather\nthan semantic lookup — worth noting, since a string-named symbol is exactly the case grep\ncatches and the LSP misses.)\n\nDestructive repair reaches identity at:\n\n```\nsrc/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py:114-115\n    root = Path(config.repo_root(repo_root))\n    who = identity._git_email(root)\n```\n\n4 candidate sites surfaced, and all 4 are false positives on inspection — none reaches\n`_git_email` against an unredirected `repo_root`:\n\n| Site | Why it does not reach |\n|---|---|\n| `test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py:68` | validates a blank reason before any operational work |\n| `test_doctor.py:573` (dry-run) | never enters `run_repair` |\n| `test_doctor.py:746` (non-blocking store) | no repair findings to act on |\n| `test_doctor_locks.py:564` | the lock path does not repair |\n\nAll 4 pass: `8 passed in 1.18s`. **Result set: empty**, recorded as the AC requires.\n\n### AC6 — `make verify` green: MET via CI, tagged `[non-codebase]`\n\nThe authoritative signal is CI's `Verified` vote, not a local run — `make test` selects\nexactly what CI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell selects, and a change cannot merge\nwithout `Verified +1`. Queried live:\n\n```\n$ curl -s --user admin:*** \\\n  \".../a/changes/?q=I842850e989f3b3e1c91bc2499e46800efbaa4b6a&o=DETAILED_LABELS\"\nchange 2983 MERGED | tests: make doctor repair identity hermetic\n    LLM-Review [(None, 1)]\n    Verified   [(None, 1)]\n```\n\nLocal substitutes were also run green on `origin/main`: `make lint` (ruff check + format,\n2791 files, zizmor, actionlint) `RC=0`, and `make typecheck` `Success: no issues found in\n771 source files`.\n\nOne methodological note worth keeping: the first `make lint` pass was dirty because a\nthrowaway verification worktree had been created *inside* `.rebar/scratch`, so lint scanned\nit too. Nested worktrees are inside the lint tree — put them outside it.\n\n### Unverified remainder\n\nA full local `make verify` on this host was deliberately not run, because a concurrent\nverify was already occupying the box and the CI vote is the stronger evidence. That is the\nwhole of the gap."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789924837092229950,"uuid":"17d8f4ce-632c-4ef9-aaf7-20280496662d"}